@@ -130,6 +130,20 @@ The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each hold
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse view: a specialty directory listing every specialty it knows, each with the veterinarians who hold it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each specialty appears under its stored name, and each veterinarian appears by full name, first name then last name. All specialties fit on one page. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears under none, so the page is not a full roster. The view is read-only, and it is reached by its address alone, with no link from any other page.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name on a single page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding a specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian is listed under it by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding several specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian is listed under each of them.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+
